table displaystyle=\"true\" columnalign=\"right left\" columnspacing=\"0em\" rowspacing=\"0.8em 0.8em 0.8em\"><mtr><mtd><mi>n</mi><mi>p</mi></mtd><mtd><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4.5</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi></mi><mo>≯</mo><mn>5.</mn><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace></mstyle><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle mathcolor=\"red\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo>×</mo></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>\nSo, we <em>cannot</em> use the normal approximation of the binomial distribution.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Therefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"</p>\n</div></div>",
